<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλπις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, ἡ, acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλπιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.20
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλπιδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					6.40
				</span></i>
			:—<i>pitcher</i> (Thess. word for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρία</span>, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				1095
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> and Pi.Il.cc., <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				107
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				123
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1339
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lys.</u>
				358
			</span></i>, etc.; a kind of <i>cup</i>, Philem.Gr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.468f
			</span></i>; <i>box</i> for unguent, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				106.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.25.17
			</span></i>; <i>urn for drawing lots</i> or <i>collecting votes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				57
			</span></i>; <i>cinerary urn</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				53
			</span></i>: with play on the original sense, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.74
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				7.384
			</span></i> (Marc. Arg.); <i>Panathenaic vase</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				122
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλπη</span>
			 (B) <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gem.
				3.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				5.92
			</span></i> :—in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλπη</span></b> , ἡ (q.v.), and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλπος</span></b> , ὁ.</div>
